// Intake evaluation set (A05, issue #9; plan 22 section 10).
//
// SYNTHETIC DATA. Every utterance here was written for this repository. None of
// it is real customer text, no line came from HUTCH traffic, and no MSISDN,
// name or NIC appears in any of it (I13, I16).
//
// Gold labels are the intent the utterance *means*, by the taxonomy in
// clarity.modules.conversation.intents. They are deliberately NOT derived from
// the keyword patterns in conversation/service.py. A set written by reading the
// matcher would score the matcher against itself and always agree, which is the
// same mistake the authorization parity suite made before M-IAM fixed it. So
// several lines below are phrasings a customer would plainly use that the
// current keyword intake gets wrong, and they are supposed to be there.
//
// `language` is what the line is written in, declared by the author. It is not
// the output of detect_language, because that detector is one of the things
// being measured and cannot also be the source of truth. Note that `si-en`
// (Singlish, romanised Sinhala) has no script of its own, so detect_language
// reports it as `en` today; Singlish intake is C04 (issue #23).
//
// Seed set: 20 per language. Plan 22 section 10 requires 300 per language, so
// the intake gate reports UNEVALUABLE until the set is grown. The F1 is still
// computed and reported, so the shortfall and the score are both visible.
{"id": "intake-si-001", "language": "si", "text": "මගේ ගිණුමෙන් රුපියල් 49ක් කැපී ගියේ ඇයි?", "intent": "BALANCE_DEDUCTION_QUERY", "slots": {"amount_lkr": "49"}}
